[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Argument Matchers in Mockito"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"When writing unit tests with Mockito, verifying interactions and stubbing method behaviors often require flexible argument matching. Argument matchers allow you to specify ranges or patterns of arguments rather than exact values."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The Golden Rule of Mockito Matchers"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"A crucial rule to remember when using Mockito argument matchers is that ALL arguments must be provided as matchers if any argument uses a matcher. Mixing raw values and matchers in the same method call will throw an InvalidUseOfMatchersException."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"// Incorrect
when(service.process(anyString(), 5)).thenReturn(true);

// Correct
when(service.process(anyString(), eq(5))).thenReturn(true);"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Commonly Used Argument Matchers"},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"any(): Matches any object, including null."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"anyInt(), anyString(), anyList(): Specific data type matchers that improve readability."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"eq(): Used when you need to mix an exact primitive or object value with other matchers."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"isNull() / notNull(): Matches null or non-null arguments respectively."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Practical Example"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"public class OrderServiceTest {
    @Test
    public void testOrderProcessing() {
        PaymentService paymentService = mock(PaymentService.class);
        OrderService orderService = new OrderService(paymentService);

        // Stubbing with matchers
        when(paymentService.charge(anyString(), anyDouble())).thenReturn(true);

        boolean result = orderService.checkout("ORD-123", 99.99);

        assertTrue(result);
        verify(paymentService).charge(eq("ORD-123"), anyDouble());
    }
}"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Argument matchers provide immense flexibility for complex test scenarios. Always remember to wrap exact values with eq() when combining them with other matchers to keep your test suites robust and error-free."}]
